{"id": "EUVD-2026-59496", "enisaUuid": "10de6fa6-9aa5-3196-9a9e-85c8f450132a", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nocfs2: reject FITRIM ranges shorter than a cluster\n\nocfs2_trim_mainbm() trims the global bitmap in cluster units, but its\ntoo-short range validation only checks sb->s_blocksize.\n\nOn filesystems with a cluster size larger than the block size, a FITRIM\nrange that is at least one block but shorter than one cluster is accepted\nand shifted down to len == 0.  The later start + len - 1 and len -= ... \narithmetic then underflows and can drive trimming past the requested\nrange.\n\nReject ranges shorter than s_clustersize instead.  That preserves the\nexisting -EINVAL behavior for requests that cannot discard even one\nallocation unit and keeps zero-cluster trims out of the group walk.", "datePublished": "2026-08-15T05:58:36", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-16T18:55:34", "baseScore": 7.1, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d903d59c0315f59bdf0214b4f13d71c9feb2c45c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/441abb77222f155e8d931dbabb465466db01cfd7", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e652d0f5108e447b22da4249bcd23dd1b63c73dd", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/346314bb0cc2fc52b50b73d6ecc62e0217455c2e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/06c0a0431b9856506fcd9b2c1b0c6136567d756d", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/3fa7139b5f42731a61f78c42433adae13f9adc21", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2c13e02592b918be7725ab5965e01ef4e46c4b57", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ca1afd88f5eaaff9168e1466e5401385edf59543"], "aliases": ["GHSA-xvwx-4pm6-jf3g", "CVE-2026-74349"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.13, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "07bfcb49-73fb-3c25-b2d6-83a1e1be6278", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "aa89762c54800208d5afdcd8e6bf124818f17fe0 <ca1afd88f5eaaff9168e1466e5401385edf59543"}, {"id": "07f9c03a-b5d0-3b38-9310-2490421d94b4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.97"}, {"id": "1ae078ea-8076-395d-b762-8743c0685be4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.40"}, {"id": "44cfe0a3-8dd6-3b15-ac77-512531901de1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "aa89762c54800208d5afdcd8e6bf124818f17fe0 <06c0a0431b9856506fcd9b2c1b0c6136567d756d"}, {"id": "4d6465bd-ae01-3d5c-83ae-e9f000729e7f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "aa89762c54800208d5afdcd8e6bf124818f17fe0 <d903d59c0315f59bdf0214b4f13d71c9feb2c45c"}, {"id": "5445d417-cad2-321b-9e83-bdca5a2ad49d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.10.261"}, {"id": "5f912661-ccaf-33bd-8695-b09068b95d50", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.1.178"}, {"id": "5fe3e29a-8028-3067-a24f-02f4ba2becc9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.1.5"}, {"id": "60b81607-3e42-36c2-9515-5b9f095ce83c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "aa89762c54800208d5afdcd8e6bf124818f17fe0 <441abb77222f155e8d931dbabb465466db01cfd7"}, {"id": "82c258d8-0334-39a6-b566-4f56149add0f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "890ae7e8-6e23-37e9-98bb-7c15072cce7b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "3.14"}, {"id": "9dc92cc1-9a1c-3b9f-add7-93f75b5d5a53", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "aa89762c54800208d5afdcd8e6bf124818f17fe0 <346314bb0cc2fc52b50b73d6ecc62e0217455c2e"}, {"id": "a6a1059f-62ea-3aab-8153-3e58aff416d9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "aa89762c54800208d5afdcd8e6bf124818f17fe